From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:45:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 151/342] meson_i2c: header pins through meson_header; I2C B
 for programs

I2C A's pins (the RTC shield's) are claimed in meson_header. I2C B, on
header pins 27 and 28, is the programs' bus: its device tree node is
disabled, and it was left unattached. It now attaches, gets no scan at
boot, and publishes /dev/bus/i2c/header: the first open file claims and
muxes its pins (B_BUSY while a program has one as GPIO), the last one
closed gives them back as GPIO. An ioctl runs one transfer: the bytes
written, a repeated start and the bytes read, or only the address, to
see whether a device answers. Until a program has the bus open, the bus
manager's bus_raw device can't use it either.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
